# Sentinel Ultra — Environment & Git

## Never

Edit tracked source files under `environment/repo/`. That breaks PR grounding.

## Fixable Dockerfile / env issues

- Alpine missing bash → `apk add --no-cache bash`
- Missing `frozen-requirements.txt` when Dockerfile COPYs it → generate
- Missing `tmux` / `asciinema` → install
- `FROM ...:latest` → pin concrete tag
- Low cpus/memory/storage → bump within task.toml limits
- Bad shebang, CRLF, non-executable scripts → normalize
- Stray root artifacts (`metadata.json`, wrong language labels) → clean

## Not Fixable env

- Tangled apt/pip/npm/cargo toolchain conflicts
- External multi-GB / live service deps at build or solve (vendoring one small file can be fixable)
- Oracle timeout may try bump; otherwise may be Not Fixable

## Git hygiene (usually Fixable)

Do work inside `environment/repo`, then re-zip. HEAD wins over mismatched `base_commit_sha` — realign toml to HEAD.

Must be clean before upload:

```bash
git rev-parse --verify HEAD          # resolves
git rev-parse HEAD                   # == base_commit_sha
git rev-list --all --not HEAD        # empty (no leaked fix history)
git remote                           # empty
git config --local --get-regexp '^filter\.'   # empty
git status --porcelain               # empty
# no .git/logs; .git < 100 MB
git apply --check ../../tests/tests.patch
```

## Runtime network

Build may use network. Agent: allowlist gateway only. Verifier: airgapped (`no-network`).
